WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.476 --> 00:00:03.877
"Rosie!" Mom called.

2
00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:06.600
"We're waiting!"

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.544
Rosie was juggling some tennis balls.

4
00:00:11.584 --> 00:00:14.407
"Coming!" she answered.

5
00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:32.629
Rosie's brother Zack had a piano lesson today.

6
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.831
After that, their brother Jimmy had a baseball game.

7
00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:41.694
thought Rosie.

8
00:00:41.714 --> 00:00:44.235
"It'll be a long morning.

9
00:00:45.556 --> 00:00:48.457
Maybe I can practice during the boys' activities."

10
00:00:49.497 --> 00:00:51.118
She put the balls in her backpack.

11
00:00:52.139 --> 00:00:54.200
Then she ran outside to the car.

12
00:01:00.136 --> 00:01:01.277
Zack was annoyed.

13
00:01:01.297 --> 00:01:03.579
"What took you so long, Rosie?"

14
00:01:03.599 --> 00:01:08.382
"I know what she was doing," Jimmy said.

15
00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:11.584
"She was practicing again."

16
00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:15.007
Zack laughed.

17
00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:19.670
"Rosie, you can't even catch one ball!

18
00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.711
You'll never learn how to juggle!"

19
00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:24.613
Rosie's cheeks turned pink.

20
00:01:26.255 --> 00:01:27.956
Zack was a talented piano player.

21
00:01:30.528 --> 00:01:32.689
Jimmy was the best hitter on his baseball team.

22
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:35.991
Rosie wanted to have a talent too.

23
00:01:36.011 --> 00:01:40.813
"I just have to keep practicing," she thought.

24
00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:49.557
Later the family was having a snack.

25
00:01:50.657 --> 00:01:52.358
Suddenly they heard a boom!

26
00:01:53.199 --> 00:01:55.700
"Thunder!" said Jimmy.

27
00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:03.597
Outside, rain poured down and lightning flashed.

28
00:02:04.618 --> 00:02:07.779
Inside, the lights flickered and then went out.

29
00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:09.799
Zack groaned.

30
00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:12.981
"We just lost our electricity."

31
00:02:20.663 --> 00:02:22.324
Mom went to call the electric company.

32
00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.841
"No TV."

33
00:02:31.842 --> 00:02:32.562
Jimmy sighed.

34
00:02:32.582 --> 00:02:36.544
"No computer," Zack grumbled.

35
00:02:36.564 --> 00:02:39.405
"This is so boring."

36
00:02:41.546 --> 00:02:43.146
Rosie reached into her backpack.

37
00:02:45.807 --> 00:02:47.068
She took a deep breath.

38
00:02:47.748 --> 00:02:51.890
She tossed one, two, three balls into the air.

39
00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.271
"You're juggling!"

40
00:02:55.732 --> 00:02:56.332
Zack cried.

41
00:02:57.612 --> 00:02:58.333
Jimmy clapped.

42
00:02:58.353 --> 00:02:59.253
"You did it!"

43
00:03:04.697 --> 00:03:06.878
The boys watched Rosie juggle the tennis balls.

44
00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:14.403
Then she got some oranges and juggled those too.

45
00:03:14.423 --> 00:03:17.685
"Can you teach us how to juggle?"

46
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:18.766
asked Zack.

47
00:03:18.786 --> 00:03:22.569
"Sure." Rosie grinned.

48
00:03:22.589 --> 00:03:25.110
"I finally have a talent."

49
00:03:26.131 --> 00:03:27.192
Jimmy shook his head.

50
00:03:27.804 --> 00:03:29.307
"You have two talents."

51
00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:31.792
"Two?" said Rosie.

52
00:03:31.812 --> 00:03:33.776
"Yep," said Jimmy.

53
00:03:33.796 --> 00:03:37.243
"Juggling—and working hard!"
